{"tool_name":"pandora","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"pandora","home":"http://www.pandora.cs.huji.ac.il","summary":"The PANDORA web server integrates annotations for the biological analysis of sets of genes, proteins or peptides.","addition_date":"2017-03-25T12:40:33Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:12:59.515940Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"collections":["Proteomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:pandora","credit":[{"name":"Webmaster","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.skarsenty.com/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.pandora.cs.huji.ac.il/help.php"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Differential protein expression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3741"},{"term":"Enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3501"},{"term":"Gene set testing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3224"},{"term":"Protein structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2406"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2403"}]}],"name":"PANDORA","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkq320","metadata":{"abstract":"Derivation of biological meaning from large sets of proteins or genes is a frequent task in genomic and proteomic studies. Such sets often arise from experimental methods including large-scale gene expression experiments and mass spectrometry (MS) proteomics. Large sets of genes or proteins are also the outcome of computational methods such as BLAST search and homology-based classifications. We have developed the PANDORA web server, which functions as a platform for the advanced biological analysis of sets of genes, proteins, or proteolytic peptides. First, the input set is mapped to a set of corresponding proteins. Then, an analysis of the protein set produces a graph-based hierarchy which highlights intrinsic relations amongst biological subsets, in light of their different annotations from multiple annotation resources. PANDORA integrates a large collection of annotation sources (GO, UniProt Keywords, InterPro, Enzyme, SCOP, CATH, Gene-3D, NCBI taxonomy and more) that comprise ~200 000 different annotation terms associated with ~3.2 million sequences from UniProtKB. Statistical enrichment based on a binomial approximation of the hypergeometric distribution and corrected for multiple hypothesis tests is calculated using several background sets, including major gene-expression DNA-chip platforms. Users can also visualize either standard or user-defined binary and quantitative properties alongside the proteins. PANDORA 4.2 is available at http://www.pandora.cs.huji.ac.il. \u00a9 The Author(s) 2010. Published by Oxford University Press.","authors":[{"name":"Fromer M."},{"name":"Linial M."},{"name":"Rappoport N."},{"name":"Schweiger R."}],"citationCount":9,"date":"2010-05-05T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"PANDORA: Analysis of protein and peptide sets through the hierarchical integration of annotations"},"pmcid":"PMC2896089","pmid":"20444873"}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene and protein families","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0623"},{"term":"Proteins","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0078"},{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"PANDORA","home":"https://bio.tools/pandora","summary":"The PANDORA web server integrates annotations for the biological analysis of sets of genes, proteins or peptides.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:pandora/web/www.pandora.cs.huji.ac.il","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/li